*> Host variables of embedded SQL: INTO sets them, every other place
*> reads them. :RECORD.FIELD qualifies a field by its record.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. ORDERSQL.
DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
    EXEC SQL INCLUDE SQLCA END-EXEC.
01  ORDER-ROW.
    05  ORDER-ID        PIC X(10).
    05  ORDER-TOTAL     PIC S9(7)V99 COMP-3.
01  TOTAL-IND           PIC S9(4) COMP.
01  MIN-TOTAL           PIC S9(7)V99 COMP-3 VALUE 100.
01  ROW-COUNT           PIC S9(9) COMP.
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
    EXEC SQL
        DECLARE BIG CURSOR FOR
        SELECT ID, TOTAL FROM ORDERS WHERE TOTAL > :MIN-TOTAL
    END-EXEC
    EXEC SQL OPEN BIG END-EXEC
    EXEC SQL
        FETCH BIG INTO :ORDER-ROW.ORDER-ID,
                       :ORDER-TOTAL :TOTAL-IND
    END-EXEC
    EXEC SQL
        UPDATE ORDERS SET STATUS = 'B' WHERE ID = :ORDER-ID
    END-EXEC
    EXEC SQL SET :ROW-COUNT = 1 END-EXEC
    IF SQLCODE NOT = 0 OR TOTAL-IND < 0
        DISPLAY SQLERRMC ROW-COUNT ORDER-TOTAL
    END-IF
    EXEC SQL CLOSE BIG END-EXEC
    STOP RUN.
